WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:10.940
In summer 2018, Secretary of Education
Betsy DeVos announced new guidelines on

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:14.940
a provision of the federal student loan
program known as "borrower defense to

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:19.770
repayment." DeVos fixed a bizarre piece of
Obama era guidance which allowed the

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:23.939
Secretary of Education to grant
across-the-board loan forgiveness to

00:00:23.939 --> 00:00:29.029
all borrowers in a program, even to those
who could not show any evidence of harm.

00:00:29.029 --> 00:00:33.600
Predictably, Devos's move was met with
the usual hysteria, but these critiques

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:38.430
were both inaccurate and unfair. After
all, the whole point is that it's not

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:41.980
clear that all borrowers seeking loan
forgiveness actually have been

00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:46.440
defrauded. And since the Obama rules made
no meaningful effort to distinguish

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:51.360
between accidental misinformation and
deliberate fraud, colleges were about to

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:56.309
become pinatas for target hungry lawyers,
with taxpayers stuck footing the bill.

00:00:56.309 --> 00:01:01.760
DeVos got this one right. The new
rules make more sense for colleges, tax

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:05.020
payers, and students willing to repay
their debts.

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:08.300
How do you think we should

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:13.260
best balance the needs of student
borrowers and taxpayers? Let us know in

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:18.090
your comments. Also, let us know what
other topics you'd like our scholars to

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:23.340
cover in 60 seconds, and be sure to like
and subscribe for more research and

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:27.439
videos from AEI.

